# Used by run-https.bat / run-https.sh (the no-Docker release). Caddy
# terminates TLS - fetching and renewing a Let's Encrypt certificate
# automatically - and reverse-proxies everything to the eeck server, which
# run-https binds to 127.0.0.1 only so it is never reachable except through
# this proxy. Same idea as this repo's own Caddyfile (used by
# docker-compose.tls.yml), just pointed at a local port instead of a
# container name.
#
# `storage` is set explicitly to a folder next to this file rather than
# Caddy's own default (under the running user's home directory): the
# systemd unit (eeck-caddy.service.template) locks that directory away with
# ProtectHome, and a relative path here resolves the same way whether this
# runs from systemd (WorkingDirectory=/opt/eeck) or by hand from wherever
# the release folder was unpacked.
{
	storage file_system {
		root ./caddy-data
	}
}

{$EECK_DOMAIN} {
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:{$EECK_PORT}
}
